C. DISCREPANCY EXPLANATION:
   Ultralytics defaults: (a) conf=0.001 near-zero threshold, (b) IoU=NMS=0.6, (c) max_det=300,
   (d) their own internal 101-point interpolation, (e) val vs test split, and (f) class mapping
   they infer from the data.yaml (uses dataset names but their API returns dataset indices).
   PROJECT CUSTOM CALIBRATED protocol: (a) VAL-only 4D sweep -> conf=0.70 + match_IoU=0.40,
   (b) POSITIONAL class decoding (DEFECT_MODEL_INDEX_TO_CANONICAL), (c) per-class greedy IoU,
   (d) all-point VOC/COCO monotone interpolation, (e) LOCKED TEST split reported after calibrate.
   The 2~2.5pp mAP50 gap between these two reports IS EXPECTED given the threshold/protocol diffs.
   We use CUSTOM CALIBRATED numbers and disclose the protocol in every metric artifact.
